## Context

Author rule (0416, absolute): a project name is never synthesized —
parentage and identity are data, not inference. 0416 (PR #760) removed
the last name-parsing from the HDM chain, but `GEM_aggregate.py` still
parses/normalizes names, and nothing prevents name synthesis from
creeping back in.

## Quoi faire

1. Adherence ratchet: no name-derivation operations (regex/split/strip
   building a Name value) in data/reference/*.py outside an allowlist;
   start with GEM_aggregate.py allowlisted-with-comment (its rework is
   0429, OUT of preprint perimeter) so the ratchet covers the HDM/v2
   chain immediately and tightens when 0429 lands.
2. Mechanics: AST or source-grep test in tests/, @pytest.mark.adherence,
   same pattern as test_no_hardcoded_reference_path.py.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Ratchet test green on current tree, red on injected name synthesis
- [ ] GEM_aggregate.py allowlisted with reference to 0429
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Related

- 0416 (the rule, PR #760), 0429 (GEM rework inherits the ratchet),
  0419/0430 (ratchet mechanics precedents).
